<Layout title="Research & published work">
  <header class="wrap page-intro"><p class="eyebrow">Research / Published work & open questions</p><h1>Better data.<br /><span>More trustworthy models.</span></h1><p class="lead">I’m interested in how machine learning can remain useful when data comes from different sources, carries sensitive information, and reflects uneven real-world conditions.</p><p>My intended direction is data science and AI in healthcare. I bring experience in operational data engineering and experimental machine learning, and I’m seeking opportunities to develop that foundation through research.</p></header>
  <section class="wrap section research-publication" aria-labelledby="publication"><div><p class="eyebrow">Published / 2022</p><h2 id="publication">A Review on E-Banking Security in Bangladesh: An Empirical Study</h2><p class="authors">Md. Ahosan Hossain Sijan · Arshad Shahoriar · <strong>Md. Salimullah</strong> · Ankan Shahriar Islam · Razib Hayat Khan</p><p>Proceedings of the 2nd International Conference on Computing Advancements (ICCA 2022), pp. 330–336.</p><p>Co-authored work on security in Bangladesh’s e-banking context. It provides an early foundation in examining a socio-technical problem through academic research.</p><div class="link-row"><a class="button" href="https://doi.org/10.1145/3542954.3543002">Read publication <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="text-link" href="https://dblp.org/rec/conf/icca2/SijanSSIK22">Bibliographic record ↗</a><a class="text-link" href={pathTo('publication.bib')} download>Download citation ↓</a></div></div><aside class="publication-aside"><span class="eyebrow">Publication record</span><p class="publication-year">2022</p><dl><dt>Type</dt><dd>Co-authored conference paper</dd><dt>DOI</dt><dd class="mono">10.1145/3542954.3543002</dd><dt>Verification</dt><dd>Public bibliographic record</dd></dl></aside></section>
  <section class="wrap section" aria-labelledby="research-experience"><p class="eyebrow">Research experience</p><h2 id="research-experience">Work in progress, with boundaries.</h2><div class="research-rows"><article><span class="tag">Experimental work</span><h3>Encrypted traffic classification</h3><p>Investigating deep learning approaches to encrypted network traffic, including CNN, recurrent, Transformer, and hybrid architectures. Topics include packet-level representations, class imbalance, and comparative evaluation across QUIC, Orange’20, and ISCXVPN2016 datasets.</p><p class="small">This is experimental work described in my research record. No benchmark result or publication status is claimed here; reproducible code, dataset licences, and evaluation protocols are required before releasing results.</p></article><article><span class="tag">Exploratory collaboration</span><h3>Elitelab.ai</h3><p>Research collaboration from March 2025, as recorded in my professional dossier. Areas explored include federated learning, privacy-preserving machine learning, explainable AI, and possible healthcare applications, alongside industry perspectives and research-intern evaluation.</p><p class="small">Exploration and collaboration are distinct from completed experiments or published healthcare research.</p></article></div></section>
  <section class="practice-section"><div class="wrap section"><p class="eyebrow">Intended research direction</p><h2>Questions I want to investigate.</h2><div class="question-grid"><article><h3>Heterogeneous data</h3><p>How do differences in source populations, missingness, and data representation affect a model’s generalisation across healthcare datasets?</p></article><article><h3>Privacy & collaboration</h3><p>What trade-offs emerge when institutions collaborate on learning while keeping sensitive records within their own boundaries?</p></article><article><h3>Trust & reproducibility</h3><p>How can data lineage, explicit evaluation protocols, and understandable model behaviour support reliable decision support?</p></article></div><p class="small">These are future research interests. I do not claim clinical experience or deployed healthcare prediction systems.</p></div></section>
  <section class="wrap contact-band"><p class="eyebrow">For prospective supervisors & collaborators</p><h2>Let’s discuss a<br />well-defined research question.</h2><p>I’m interested in rigorous supervision, reproducible experiments, and research that takes data quality seriously.</p><a class="button" href={pathTo('contact/')}>Contact me about research ↗</a></section>
</Layout>
